Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the vsavjw catalogue entry re-pointed to merged-m22
 (14z-189)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

jtframe's .rom builder locates every zip member by CRC32 and by nothing else
(mra2rom.go:163-172, no name fallback), so the machine entry must name the
CRCs of the actual build or the MRA produces no .rom at all. Regenerated from
build/m3b_merged30/rompath/vsavjw.zip by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py in the
consuming tree; --check now reports the catalogue matches the build.

EIGHT members moved, and they are the M22 delta exactly (the consuming tree's
build/agent189/m22/deltas2.txt and opset_and_gain.txt):
  vm3j.03d  e537ef29 -> 09d90dbd   program: #195's two sites — the hit-time
                                   class write (0x01868C) and the knockdown
                                   tail (0x024D92, pad 0x024D98)
  vm3j.04d  d522cfe7 -> b24a648b   program: placement shifted by #195's chain
  vm3j.07b  8f131ac1 -> 548977d5   and tail thunk; #194's one byte in the
  vm3j.10b  b1a24511 -> 49fdef4d   placed Cosmo record; every relocation
  vsw.41    02991388 -> 21e69247   target content-identical
  vsw.42    5b75ebbd -> bb7d6f89
  vsw.33m   27a0fd82 -> ee1148dd   group-C glyphs, the M21 -> M22 mark
  vsw.37m   b759cc68 -> 11ff7862   likewise

No RTL, no cfg, no core change: doc/mame.xml only. cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and
cores/cps15 remain byte-untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XPP3MSbSJVQCQKEQX5qsoX
